build: bump QEMU to rebased ast-v5_5_0-branch

Rebase our QEMU changes onto the current upstream ast-v5_5_0-branch
(RD-SW/qemu); upstream had been rebased onto a far newer QEMU base, so our
old fork shared only an ancient merge base. The fork now carries two commits
on the new tip:

- honor -object memory-backend-file for DRAM, re-patched for upstream's new
  DRAM/DRAM_EXT split: machine->ram is aliased into both windows.
- add SimControl exit device at 0xe0080000 (andesim_ctrl_ops).

Dropped the stale "Fix for server04" commit (two server04 build hacks plus
an obsolete semihosting guestfd map -- andesim no longer uses semihosting).
The hotloops plugin is now built out-of-tree (previous commit).

